  "question": {
    "text": "A person pushes a box on a rough horizontal plateform surface. He applies a force of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>N</mi></math> over a distance of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi></math>. Thereafter, he gets progressively tired and his applied force reduces linearly with distance to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>N</mi></math>. The total distance through which the box has been moved is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi></math>. What is the work done by the person during the total movement of the box?"
  },
